# Best-props list (active sports)

When ranking or locking **Standard Over / Standard Under / Goblin** plays for a slate, always output **four sections**: WNBA, MLB, Soccer, Tennis.

- **Best-props answer:** directional **L5 = 5** only (printed 5/0). A 4/1 face stays off the reply even though the pipeline list gate is still L5>=4. If a sport has no 5/0 face, say so in that section.
- Do not skip a sport because the pool is thin. If nothing clears L5=5, say so in that section.
- Soccer/tennis often store hits in `last5_over` / `last5_under` (not `l5_over`). Use those when `l5_over` is empty.
- **Hard list gate:** directional L5 >= 4; Goblins Over-only; no Demons. **WNBA / WNBA1H / WNBA1Q** list + Flex require directional **L5 = 5** for Standard OVER, Standard UNDER, and Goblin OVER (L5>=4 is not listed). **MLB** uses keep props 1–10 (same gates as Goblin-70); MLB Standard stays off. League tickets (MLB, WNBA, NBA, NHL, NFL, CFB, including preseason and period slates) allow an ESPN regular-season event. MLB and WNBA postseason (ESPN season type 3, including WNBA period slates) is allowed, priced at the cell minus 3 points, tagged postseason=1, graded on gated_goblin_postseason, and kept out of the 71/127 book, one slip a day until 30 are graded. Preseason stays blocked. Unknown game type stays blocked. NFL, CFB, NBA, NHL, and CBB postseason stay blocked. Blocked legs have no cell and do not fall back to the 0.763 floor. **Tennis** Goblin OVER uses keep gates in `utils/tennis_keep_gates.py`: Games Won on corrected board-opponent attaches: ungated 819/1224 (66.9%), discount keep 72/99 (72.7%, band 64%–82%). The old 83% n=331 and 76.3% catalog were wrong-match inflated; the discount cell does not separate from 67% or 76%. Price cap stays 0.62 until a new graded week moves that band. Total Games keep on corrected attaches is 146/208 (70.2%, band 64%–76%); ungated corrected is 665/1050 (63.3%). The old 78.7% n=61 was wrong-match inflated. Price Goblin Total Games at 70.2%. No D. Tennis Standard UNDER Aces / Double Faults is **off** after serve-actual backfill (pre-~90% was missing→0 inflation; post-backfill ~57% / ~29%). Tennis Standard OVER Games Won: L10>=8+(L5gap>=5 | L5 2nd-won%>=45.7). Other tennis Standard / Goblin Aces/DF stay off. **Soccer** uses keep props in `utils/soccer_keep_gates.py`: Shots L5=5+L10>=8 (76% n=21); SOT L5>=4+Off (68% n=68; Off = STARTER or HIGH_VOL or top-3); Saves are off tickets. Goblin 1.5 is 205/343 (59.8%, band 55–65%), under the ~77% a 3-leg at 2.2x needs. The L5>=4 cell 21/26 (80.8%) is not a price. Own-defense stays off (within a line the tier split is thin; shots-on-target faced does not follow the goals-conceded tier). Opponent attack is retired. List entry is L5>=4 plus settlement only. Fade Goals / G+A / assists / fouls / volume props. Soccer Standard O/U uses the same per-prop **list** gates. **Ticket** SOT still needs directional L5=5 on top of that pool entry (L5>=4 is list-only). Saves stay off tickets. Thin-history competitions (`utils/competition_history.py` on `league`): block tags like WORLDCUP* with too little prior depth — not a hardcoded tournament list. **CFB** uses keep props in `utils/cfb_keep_gates.py`: Goblin OVER Rush Attempts / Kicking Points off the list (33%/20% ungated). Player TDs stay on the L5>=4 list but are faded from the L5=5 ticket stack. Standard Rec Yards UNDER stays on the list but is blocked from the cover-stack ticket path. Pass Yards Goblin OVER list stays L5>=4; badge and tickets both skip D via `cfb_pass_yards_goblin_skip_d` (D is N/A, not a Silver miss).
- **NFLP (preseason) exception:** 2025 L5 / snap% is starter volume, not tonight. Week-3 starters sit or play 1 series — do not list Sit/cameo skill **overs** even with L5 4+ (tiny cameo lines like pass 25.5 still drop). Backup QBs play the bulk (Q2–Q4); 2025 snap 40–70% is a spot start, not tonight’s cameo. Backup skill overs need D (Weak|Below Avg); L5 is not required. Kickers still use L5 >= 4. **Regular-season NFL (League=NFL)** list gate stays directional L5≥4. Sep-1 current-season filtering is for **honest sample flags** (`THIN_*` / `games_used`) — not a ban on using last-season or preseason boxes when judging face consistency. D stays a veto on NFLP skill overs into Elite | Above Avg | Avg.
- **Goblin / Standard face preference (manual + list builds):** The ranker may still print L5>=4. The best-props reply keeps **L5=5** only. **WNBA / WNBA1H / WNBA1Q** were already L5=5 only. **Do not play 3/2 (or worse) faces**. That L5 window **may include last season and NFL preseason** — it does not have to be current-season-only. Prefer the **deepest Goblin** that still clears L5≥4 over a near-Standard Goblin that only clears 3/5 (WNBA still needs L5=5). **Standards use the same L5 consistency preference**, but they **must still clear our gates and filters** (sport keep gates, ticket L5=5+L10≥8+D where required, D alignment, cover floors, MLB/tennis/soccer/CFB exceptions above) — consistency alone does not put a Standard on the card.
- **D is badge-only (not a hard filter)** except NFLP skill overs (see above). Failing D on other sports should still appear, usually as **Silver** when D is the only miss (Gold = L5 + Cover + Delta + Dir + D + Rank all pass). **Exception:** CFB/CFB1H Pass Yards Goblin OVER — D is N/A in badge logic (same `cfb_pass_yards_goblin_skip_d` as tickets); it does not cost Silver.
- **D alignment for badges (all pipeline sports — WNBA, MLB, Soccer, Tennis, NBA, CFB, CBB, NHL, NFL, etc.):**
  - Overs vs Weak | Below Avg; Unders vs Elite | Above Avg. Avg never passes D.
  - **MLB pitcher Hits Allowed / ERA / pitcher Ks:** Opp Def is opponent **offense** (hits, scoring, K-rate), mapped into the same Weak→Elite buckets. Do not use opponent team pitching for those.
  - **MLB hitter TB / H+R+RBI / hits:** opponent **pitching** (run prevention) plus player **BA**. Gate is BA>=.275 (min 80 AB). Display: **BA .312** then **Opp pitch Weak|Below** (leaky staff). Team Bat Strong|Above is labels-only.
  - **MLB hitter_strikeouts exception:** Overs vs Opp pitch Elite|Above; Unders vs Weak|Below (stingy staff → more batter Ks). Rank also inverts. Do not invert pitcher strikeouts (those stay on lineup K-rate).
  - **Tennis:** individual opponent (ATP/WTA). Same Weak|Below / Elite|Above bands. Unknown opponent does not pass D.
  - **NFL tackles / tackles_ast / solo:** Def Tier is opponent **rush offense** (`opp_rush_off_rank`), not opp pass D. Same Weak|Below OVER / Elite|Above UNDER bands (chunk rush OFF → UNDER; weak rush OFF → OVER). Soft own-D is context only. See `Sports/NFL/data/nfl_keep_fade.md`.
- **MLB Goblin OVER keep vs fade (numbered props 1–21):** Keep 1–10 on the per-prop gate below. Fade 11–21 (Runs, Singles, batter Walks, PA, RBIs, 1st-inning walks/runs, HR, 2B, 3B, SB) and all Demons / Standard (no Standard cell ≥70% at n≥40).
  - **1 Walks Allowed:** L10≥8 + Own pitch Weak|Below (leaky staff).
  - **2 Pitches Thrown:** L10≥8 + Own pitch Weak|Below.
  - **3 ERA:** Goblin 0.5 + L5=5 + L10≥8. Ban 1.5+. No rank gate.
  - **4 Pitcher Ks:** L10≥8 + Own pitch Elite|Above (stingy staff).
  - **5 Hits Allowed:** L10≥8 + Opp bats Strong|Above. Do not require own leaky pitching.
  - **6 Pitching Outs:** L10≥8 + Own pitch Elite|Above.
  - **7 H+R+RBI:** BA>=.275 + L5=5 + Opp pitch Weak|Below (80.8% n=104).
  - **8 Hitter Ks:** K%>=28 + L10≥8 + Opp pitch Elite|Above (76.6% n=325). On the Goblin list and Goblin-70 tickets.
  - **9 Hits / 10 Total Bases:** BA>=.275 + L5=5 + Opp pitch Weak|Below (71% n~170). No L10, no cover, no team Bat.
  - **Live check-in bar (not ~90% L5-gated backtest cells):** Pitcher Ks ~80%, HA ~83%, ERA ~88%, Walks ~81%, Hitter Ks ~77%, H+R+RBI/Hits/TB ~65–70%. ERA and hitter L5-gated props should hold closer to backtest; pitcher volume at ~80% is expected L10-primary cost. Grade `wind_out_hot` + L10≥8 boosts against `data/reports/mlb_pitcher_l10_primary_gates.md`.
- **Diamond / Platinum (on top of Gold):** Diamond = Gold + directional L10 >= 8 AND season HR > 70% (min 10 games vs today's line). Platinum = Gold + exactly one of those two extra gates. Remaining Gold has neither. **CFB PRIOR_SEASON_FILL / PRIOR_SEASON_L5** (weeks 0–5 last-year pad on this player's own boxes) stays Gold at most — never Diamond/Platinum. `l5_sample_n` / `games_used` stay current-season counts so a filled face L5=5 is not a clean 2026 sample.
- **Prop tier (S–D) is the market; badge is the play.** They stack. Sort S → A → B → C → D then Diamond → Platinum → Gold → Silver → Bronze. S = MLB pitcher Goblin Ks/walks/pitches/**hits allowed** (L10-primary band) and NBA1Q Goblin counting (~80%+ L5=5). A = WNBA Goblin scoring/reb+ast/FGA, NBA Goblin scoring, tennis games, soccer saves, pitching outs. WNBA Goblin PRA is B. Promotions into A/S: MLB Goblin H+R+RBI with D pass; MLB Goblin total bases with cover + D; hitter Ks with cover ≥1. Shadow cells tag as **W** and stay on the list. `scripts/rank_best_props_today.py` prints `S/Diamond`, `A/Gold*`, `W/Silver`. NBA/NHL/CBB/NFL/CFB/Golf now get letters (unlisted Goblin OVER = C, Standard = D) instead of a blank tier.
- Prefer `scripts/rank_best_props_today.py` so all four sports are generated the same way. CFB prints as an extra section when `outputs/<date>/cfb/step8_cfb_direction_clean.xlsx` exists. Golf prints as an extra section when `outputs/<date>/golf/step8_golf_direction_clean.xlsx` exists.
- **Tennis list window:** keep ET today + 2 days (slam first rounds post Saturday–Monday). Do not ranker-filter tennis down to the slate date only.
- **Tennis format:** BO5 Total Games (line > 31.5) must not list from BO3 last-5 (all games / avg < 32). Inverse of the BO3-line slam strip. If tennis step1 exists and step8 is missing, warn — do not print `(no step8 file)` as an empty slate.
- That script **must not** use a day-prior board just because it lives in the open Cursor checkout. It picks the worktree whose step1 `fetched_at` is the **slate date** (usually `PropORACLE_main_cp` after 1AM/8AM). If you rank by hand, pass `--step8-root` to that tree when this checkout's `fetched_at` is yesterday.

# Pipeline tickets (all sports)

**Live `/tickets` is always both:** Goblin-70 groups first, graded-main mixer under. Builder `scripts/build_goblin70_tickets.py --write-web` merges from the grade pool so a refresh cannot wipe STRONG / MLB Goblin OVER / tennis mixer groups. 9AM / 10:30 / 1PM / 4:30 refetches rebuild Goblin-70 and patch mixer **lines**; they do not drop mixer slips that left the live board.

**70% ticket engine (top of the card):** Goblin OVER and Standard Over/Under that clear the same gate (except MLB and most tennis Standard). Hard gates: directional **L5 = 5**, directional **L10 >= 8**, **and directional D** (OVER Weak|Below Avg; UNDER Elite|Above Avg; Avg/unknown fail; MLB hitter Ks invert). **WNBA Goblin PRA** also needs Off (usage HIGH/STAR or minutes HIGH) on top of that (80.6% n=36). **WNBA Goblin Rebounds 3.5+** skips D (keep L5=5+L10>=8+cover; <=2.5 still needs D). **WNBA Goblin Assists 2.5** is off tickets (1.5 stays). **WNBA Goblin Assists** with entering-game poss/g>=18 (FGA+0.44×FTA+TO) is off tickets (L5=5 64.2% n=53). **Fantasy** is off tickets for every sport (printed list already skipped it; ticket fade was WNBA-only so WNBA1Q/1H/NBA still cleared the generic stack — closed). **WNBA Goblin Points / Rebounds / Pts+Reb / Pts+Ast** also need season avg >= line+cover_unit (A-only 56–66% vs A∩B; Assists/3PM/Reb+Ast stay on plain G70 — Assists A-only 82.4% beats A∩B 76.6%). **Tennis Goblin OVER** uses keep props in `utils/tennis_keep_gates.py`: Games Won on corrected board-opponent attaches: ungated 819/1224 (66.9%), discount keep 72/99 (72.7%, band 64%–82%). Price cap stays 0.62. Total Games keep on corrected attaches is 146/208 (70.2%, band 64%–76%); ungated corrected is 665/1050 (63.3%). Price Goblin Total Games at 70.2%. No D. **Tennis Standard UNDER Aces / Double Faults** is off after serve-actual backfill (pre-~90% was missing→0 inflation). **Tennis Standard OVER Games Won** is L10>=8+(L5gap>=5 | L5 2nd-won%>=45.7). Other tennis Standard stays off. **Soccer** uses keep props in `utils/soccer_keep_gates.py`: Shots L5=5+L10>=8; SOT L5>=4+Off **list** then L5=5 **ticket**; Saves are off tickets (Goblin 1.5 is 59.8%, band 55–65%; the 80.8% n=26 cell is not a price). Own-defense stays off. Opponent attack is retired. List entry is L5>=4 plus settlement only. Other soccer props stay off. **CFB** uses keep props in `utils/cfb_keep_gates.py`: Pass Yards Goblin OVER is L5=5+cover, no D (74% ungated; D-fail 90%). L10>=8 is not a CFB gate. The face window is this season, then this player's last year, out to 8 games. Directional L8>=6 on a full 8-game window is a bonus, not a ticket block and not a new price. Player TDs fade from the L5=5 stack (0.5-line). Standard Rec Yards UNDER fades from the cover-stack (L5=5 is 0/5 vs 41% base). Standard Rush Yards UNDER keeps L5=5+D+cover. Rush Attempts / Kicking Points Goblin OVER stay off. **Golf** stays off tickets until a keep-gate cell exists (same as CBB; course-baseline projection is observe-only). **MLB Goblin OVER** uses keep props 1–10 in `utils/mlb_keep_gates.py` (pitcher Walks/Pitches/Ks/Hits Allowed/Outs = L10≥8 + D/own-pitch/opp-bats as listed; ERA 0.5 + L5=5 + L10≥8; H+R+RBI BA≥.275+L5=5+D; Hitter Ks K%≥28+L10≥8+D; Hits/TB BA≥.275+L5=5+D). MLB Standard stays off. League tickets (MLB, WNBA, NBA, NHL, NFL, CFB, including preseason and period slates) allow an ESPN regular-season event. MLB and WNBA postseason (ESPN season type 3, including WNBA period slates) is allowed, priced at the cell minus 3 points, tagged postseason=1, graded on gated_goblin_postseason, and kept out of the 71/127 book, one slip a day until 30 are graded. Preseason stays blocked. Unknown game type stays blocked. NFL, CFB, NBA, NHL, and CBB postseason stay blocked. Blocked legs have no cell and do not fall back to the 0.763 floor. Cover floor still applies on other sports (per-prop typical |last5−line| when mapped — PRA ~+3.7, FGA ~+1.1, 3s ~+0.7, NFL/CFB pass yards ~+15, rec/rush yards ~+8 — else WNBA/Tennis/NBA >= 2, Soccer/NFL unmapped >= 1). No Demons. No shadow cells. Goblin Power slips stay all-Goblin. Standard O/U that clear their keep gate ticket as their own Power 3s, not mixed onto Goblin slips. Sports: WNBA, WNBA1Q, WNBA1H, MLB, Soccer, Tennis, NBA, NBA1Q, NBA1H, NFL (regular season), CFB, CBB, WCBB, Golf, NHL. NFLP stays on its own playing-time track (sit/cameo skill overs dropped; backup skill needs D; kickers L5>=4). A sport or prop with no keep-file rule is off. NBA, CBB, and WCBB are out of season, not missing a gate. NHL is in season and has no keep gate yet (not backtested; see data/reports/nhl_goblin_gate_backtest.json), so it stays off tickets. Each keep file says whether its rule replaces the L5/L10/D stack or adds to it. Who gets in is the keep gate with the highest hit rate for that prop, and the leg must also have directional L5 = 5. Leg p is the shrunk hit rate of that gate cell, not model_prob. Three comparison tracks, flat $20, max 2 slips each. Gated Goblin is all-Goblin and is placed when N-correct is at least 1.4x; the dollar test (sweep chance times that composition's payout, minus 1) is stored and the slip is labeled EV-negative when it fails. Gated Mixed is those Goblin legs plus one Standard leg. Gated Standard is all-Standard. A Standard leg needs its own regular-season cell for that sport, prop, and direction, directional L5=5, the sport keep, and n>=30. It is priced from that cell. No cell means that track is empty for the slate. A player on one track is off the others. Cross-sport slips are allowed. MLB pitcher Goblin prices use the parent L10 cell (outs 399/498, ks 743/975, hits allowed 633/823), then postseason minus 3. Do not price those props from the L5 slice in the category file. Postseason stays on gated_goblin_postseason. One player-prop once. The same player may add a second prop and stops at 2. A sport fills its own slips first; legs that cannot fill mix across sports. Same game is allowed. Flat $20. All-Goblin 3-leg Power quotes the 25th percentile of logged scrapes (currently 1.65x, n=27, range 1.3–3.5). The old 2.3x ± 0.5 band is retired; 1.65x is below its 1.8x floor. All-Goblin 2-leg is not a fixed 1.5x: logged scrapes run 1.2x–1.5x and straddle the 1.4x floor, so that slip is scraped before submit. Mixed floors: 2-leg with 1 Goblin stays 2x until that cell has five scrapes (three remain after the July cut, lowest 2.3x, and quoting up is the unsafe direction). 3-leg with 1 Goblin and 3-leg with 2 Goblins quote the lowest scrape while the cell has fewer than five.

**Standard:** same L5=5+L10≥8+D gate as Goblin, except MLB Standard is off, tennis Standard is OVER Games Won only (L10>=8 + gap/2nd-won; UNDER Aces/DF faded after backfill), soccer Standard uses the same Shots/SOT keep gates (Saves off tickets), and CFB Standard Rec Yards UNDER is off the cover-stack (Rush Yards UNDER stays). Do not mix Standard onto Goblin Power slips. Standard slips are Power 3s from the Standard pool, as many as that pool fills.

**L5=5 shadow (`l5_only_shadow`):** directional L5=5 Goblin or Standard legs with a regular-season event, a matched event, and real actuals. DNP and minutes-unknown stay out. The sport keep gate is skipped. Price is the ungated cell (tennis Games Won 819/1224, Total Games 665/1050; other props use the category catalog). Legs and disjoint 2-leg slips are logged. They are not placed and they are not on `/tickets`. A weekly report gives the forward hit rate with a Wilson band by sport and prop, next to the gated tracks, and flags a prop only when that band's low end clears break-even at the median quote (Goblin 2-leg 1.40x, Standard 2-leg 3x). Do not wire the track into a placed gate until that forward bar is met.

Combined / graded-main (under Goblin-70) uses directional **L5 = 5** only for mixer seed and MAIN Goblin/Standard recency floors (`PROPORACLE_MAIN_*_MIN_L5_HITS` default 5). Seed order is **L5=5+D → L5=5 no-D** — L5≤4 never enters the mixer seed pool. Tennis mixer Goblins already use the keep gates above. Soccer mixer legs are Shots / SOT only (Saves off tickets; goals/G+A/assists/volume props dropped).
